{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774743,"nonce":"Pgofj4LeEV7tCeZi4fM+9M7IQLw=","title":"fix(dogfood): artifacts + results actually publish; GC stops re-warning a dangling root","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #91 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/dogfood-artifacts-and-results` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-26T15:01:20Z · Merged: 2026-07-26T17:35:40Z\n\nTwo fixes from the same dogfood session. Independent commits, so they split cleanly if you would rather review them apart.\n\n---\n\n\nThe dogfood pipeline published **no artifacts at all**, and its one result never landed. On run `019f9ec6`:\n\n```\nGET /v1/runs/{id}/artifacts              -\u003e []\nGET /v1/runs/{id}/steps/version/results  -\u003e []     # yet `version` SUCCEEDED\n```\n\n\nThe trusted egress sidecar drains `/scarab/results/\u003cname\u003e.json` and nothing else — `for f in *.json` in `docker/sidecar/scarab-results-egress.sh`, result name taken as the filename minus `.json`, contents required to be valid JSON.\n\nThe sample wrote a bare `/scarab/results/tag`. The glob matched nothing, the sidecar logged `no results to drain`, and **the step still exited 0**. So the run goes green while `${{ outputs.version.tag }}` resolves empty downstream. `deploy` would then have failed on its `test -n \"$PREV_VERSION\"` assertion — that assertion earning its place on day one.\n\nConfirmed from the live pod, not inferred: `step` and the native sidecar share the same `scarab-results` volume (sidecar read-only), `SCARAB_RESULTS_URL`/`_TOKEN` are correctly injected, and the sidecar log shows the two startup lines and no drain. The wiring was never the problem; the filename was.\n\n\n| file | result | type |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tag.json` | `outputs.version.tag` | string |\n| `commit.json` | `outputs.version.commit` | string |\n| `commits.json` | `outputs.version.commits` | number |\n\n`deploy` consumes all three and **asserts each resolved** — including that the sha is 40 chars and the count is digits, so a string *and* a number are proven to survive the round-trip rather than being echoed and believed.\n\n(`build` already emits an `image` result natively via BuildKit `--metadata-file /scarab/results/image.json` — nothing to add.)\n\n\n- `lint` tees its fmt and clippy reports (`pipefail` keeps the verdict the check's, not `tee`'s)\n- each `test` leg writes a log **named per matrix instance**, so the three legs publish three distinct artifacts instead of racing one name\n- `version` writes `version.txt` — the same facts as a file, to contrast the channels: results are small typed values the DAG interpolates, artifacts are files you download afterwards\n\n\n`dogfood_sample_compiles` now rejects any redirect into `/scarab/results/` not ending in `.json`. Verified it bites by restoring the bare form:\n\n```\nstep `version` writes result `/scarab/results/tag` — the sidecar drains\n`\u003cname\u003e.json` only, so this publishes nothing while the step still passes\n```\n\nIt inspects redirect targets only, so the comment documenting the wrong form does not trip it.\n\n\n`pipeline-syntax.mdx` documents `artifacts:` but says **nothing** about the results convention. Worth a follow-up.\n\n---\n\n\n`cas gc: root tree missing (dangling reference) — skipping` recurring on every pass.\n\n`6f7a9f1` had already fixed the real damage — a missing object used to abort the whole GC pass and wedge it forever — but only by skipping. The Db reference survived, so `gc_workspace_roots` handed the same dead hash back every pass and re-logged it indefinitely. On the local-helm dogfood that is permanent noise: runs recorded before `deploy.sh` moved the CAS onto in-cluster MinIO can never be materialized again.\n\nSelf-heal instead: a definitive `NotFound` over a **root** now clears every `output_snapshot` equal to it via a new `Db::forget_workspace_root`, covering **both** arms of the ADR-0056 mark set (`step_runs` denorm + each attempt's copy). Clearing one arm only would leave the other reporting the root and the warning would survive the fix.\n\nTwo deliberate narrowings, since this mutates run history from a GC pass:\n\n- **Roots only.** A missing *inner* tree means a parent that does exist still lists it — torn CAS, not a stale reference. Logged at `error` now instead of being lumped in with routine staleness.\n- **After the walk, never during.** A walk aborting on a transient error cannot clear anything. A failed forget is non-fatal: the sweep is still correct, next pass retries.\n\nExtends the `6f7a9f1` regression test to assert the reference is cleared and that `gc_workspace_roots` stops reporting it; confirmed the assertion bites by disabling the forget loop.\n\nAlso adds `just test-one FILTER` — the existing `test` recipe only runs the whole workspace, and CLAUDE.md says extend the recipes rather than hand-roll the Postgres env.\n\n---\n\nFull suite: **679 passed, 22 skipped.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}